# Every YAML in the build context, by name and by glob. config.yaml and
# keys.yaml hold live third-party API keys; both are bind-mounted at runtime
# and neither is ever needed at build time. The Dockerfile currently copies
# only pyproject.toml and src/, so this is belt-and-braces — but one future
# `COPY . .` would otherwise bake live keys into an image layer, where they
# survive every later `rm` and travel with every `docker push`.
config.yaml
keys.yaml
*.yaml
*.yml
